{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035998-mystery-in-nameless-war","id":1035998,"title":"Mystery in Nameless War?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-22T03:07:30-08:00","id":1035998,"title":"Mystery in Nameless War?","content":"Having free weekend, I start to wonder over my next Chronicles ideas I got prepared in 'spare time', for future games. One of which is far in future episodic game about rise of Free Council in the Nameless War from French Revolution events till the Great Refusal, with many different characters ( and players ) across span of over 110 years and around the world. ( I will probably run it after premiere of <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> to have all bolts and screws in setting. ) I would see this game as running on pulpish 'Viva la Revolution' kind of zeal, divide and cooperation in Nameless War, but with 2E <b>Mage</b> center of uncovering Mysteries - I wonder if some grand Mystery should not be behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> With other Orders, I would simply center game on the Order's Special Merit and his Supernal implications, but Libertines have <i>Techne</i> and it's... well, to varied? It's basically stating that each Sleepers technique or practice can have Supernal effects. So it's 'Oh, you can use voodoo and psychic projection as your Yantras in magic? That's great!' and Mystery is solved. It does not seem as lasting Mystery too dwell in to, at least for me now.<br /> <br /> Other idea I was having showing of Sixth Watchtower, but it seems less about Free Council and much more about 'those characters are so special they found new Path'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And here I'm in a pinch - basically, I have problem with uncovering something very 'magical' in Free Council to throw this portion of Order to players as Mystery to pull by characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. I think also on giving characters possible options of choosing Gifted or Psychics mage template alternatives from <b>Mage Chronicle's Guide</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T04:44:32-08:00","id":1036024,"title":"","content":"The big thing I think of with the Free Council and techne is that they view magic and the Supernal in a radically different way than the Diamond or Seers. I run a game in the modern LA Assembly where I like to emphasize that the Atlantis/Time Before/Exarchs mythos is only one way of interpreting magic, and it doesn't adequately explain the world on its own. The excitement and power of the Nameless is that they're living in a world dominated by people who have a very rigid and outdated and elitist perception of magic, and they can challenge their authority with things that wouldn't occur to the Atlanteanists.<br /> <br /> If you wanted a big Mystery, maybe start with some phenomenon that's big and far-reaching and subtle and exists in the blind spot of the Diamond and Seers alike, something that wouldn't make sense in a rigid Atlantean cosmology- some kind of change and growth and conflict within the Supernal Realms themselves, maybe. Then, taking a cue from the whole Locked/Linked Mystery rules on a larger scale, establish that the diverse Nameless magical traditions and Sleeper scientific and cultural practices can glimpse this Mystery in new ways by asking questions and Obsessions that wouldn't occur to (or are banned by) the Atlanteanists. No one group has all the answers, but the PCs have an incentive to seek out Nameless mages around the world and bring them into contact with each other by seeking their perspectives on this vast Mystery.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of inspiration for a framework like that. &quot;I'll show those fools at the Academy who laughed me out the door!&quot; Many scientific innovations in Europe had that kind of reaction, from natural selection to continental drift. Or something like Mass Effect where the established authorities loudly ignore the threat posed by the Reapers because it doesn't fit in their worldview, and you have to seek allies elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T05:52:40-08:00","id":1036030,"title":"","content":"The problem you're having with Techne is that you're looking at what the PCs do with it rather than why the FC uses it. The FC has observed that humanity appears to -change- the Supernal via their beliefs and rituals. They delve into Techne in order to figure out how the fuck that works. So, you have the one overarching Mystery of the FC trying to figure out the exact mechanisms that allow humanity to shape the Suprrnal. You have another set of Mysteries with the FC trying to figure out what's been changed already, or reacting to changes that they discover have been made. Finally, you have another set of Mysteries in attempting to discover what the heck humanity is going to do to the Supernal next, and can they shape it into something useful? You need to stop looking at just Techne's utilitarian ends.<br /> <br /> The 6th Watchtower is the Tremere one, the Tower of the Soul. The FC used to be a lot of very young Nameless Orders. The Tremere used to be part of the Diamond and know all the terminology and bring a sense of legitimate, long lasting history. So, what if, instead of just the Seers trying to seduce the Nameless the Tremere were as well? They could do it without having to really worry about the Diamond or Seers noticing. If you really twist their ideology in knots they even have a sort of FC view of the Supernal, they believe that slowly &quot;transforming&quot; the souls of humanity by creating a &quot;connection&quot; between those souls and the 6th Tower will eventually bring about a major change to the Supernal capable of doing things like merging all of the Subtle Arcana together into one super Arcana. Anyway, point is, the Nameless War could have had a lot of Little Refusals to various corrupting influences before getting up to the Great Refusal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:05:31-08:00","id":1036045,"title":"","content":"I'd say the Mystery is &quot;what do these Nameless Orders all have in common?&quot; Humanity is Magical isn't a mystery, it's the answer to the mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:31:17-08:00","id":1036055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035998-mystery-in-nameless-war?p=1036045#post1036045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the Mystery is &quot;what do these Nameless Orders all have in common?&quot; Humanity is Magical isn't a mystery, it's the answer to the mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>A short statement like &quot;Humanity is Magical&quot; requires unpacking and that's where the mystery lies. Considering the experiential nature of learning and understanding magic in Mage that's going to require a lot of leg work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:51:35-08:00","id":1036066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035998-mystery-in-nameless-war?p=1036055#post1036055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A short statement like &quot;Humanity is Magical&quot; requires unpacking and that's where the mystery lies. Considering the experiential nature of learning and understanding magic in Mage that's going to require a lot of leg work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was using a pithy statement to stand in for years of struggle and searching. Just wanted it to sound more dramatic. My point is that the Free Council don't start with a coherent ideology, that's the mystery they spend the 19th century on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:58:47-08:00","id":1036070,"title":"","content":"That's definitely true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:51:28-08:00","id":1036095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035998-mystery-in-nameless-war?p=1036066#post1036066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I was using a pithy statement to stand in for years of struggle and searching. Just wanted it to sound more dramatic. My point is that the Free Council don't start with a coherent ideology, that's the mystery they spend the 19th century on.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the whole global Order - sure, they need soul searching. But Order need to start from one cabal ( column in this example ) that agree on <i>some</i> dogmas. Global organizations just do not spring off thin air - they need to crystalize from some movement leaders, that rest will surely agree with. And those leaders need to know at least in part where they lead it. If 'Humanity is Magical', our Proto-FC leaders need at least to know there is Mystery about it in first place to ask those questions Libertine Creed is answer century later.<br /> <br /> Nameless War is all about various Nameless factions trying to become one coherent force ( some of them did not become FC, some even joined Seers ). So beside 'what should we do in the end', it's all those Nameless coming together. For ease of discussion, let's assume that each Nameless Order that become Free Council have their version of Techne as their special Merit. Each of our steampunks, shamans and dark revolutionist have their own Techne - and it simply <i>works</i>. Steampunks make great magical engines. shamans invoke spirits of ancestors and revolutioners are making 'magical bomb assults' (?), each working closely to their culture. They only see their end of the stick - 'my magic works better'. <b>HOW to make them question this? How to go beside their practical shtick of 'I'm good with &lt;Insert Techne&gt;'? </b>Because lonely Nameless are surely not seeing those changes on global scale as Free Council can compare notes century later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:06:23-08:00","id":1036104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035998-mystery-in-nameless-war?p=1036030#post1036030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem you're having with Techne is that you're looking at what the PCs do with it rather than why the FC uses it. The FC has observed that humanity appears to -change- the Supernal via their beliefs and rituals. They delve into Techne in order to figure out how the fuck that works. So, you have the one overarching Mystery of the FC trying to figure out the exact mechanisms that allow humanity to shape the Suprrnal. You have another set of Mysteries with the FC trying to figure out what's been changed already, or reacting to changes that they discover have been made. Finally, you have another set of Mysteries in attempting to discover what the heck humanity is going to do to the Supernal next, and can they shape it into something useful? You need to stop looking at just Techne's utilitarian ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'll just repeat myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:10:26-08:00","id":1036107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035998-mystery-in-nameless-war?p=1036030#post1036030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem you're having with Techne is that you're looking at what the PCs do with it rather than why the FC uses it. The FC has observed that humanity appears to -change- the Supernal via their beliefs and rituals. They delve into Techne in order to figure out how the fuck that works. So, you have the one overarching Mystery of the FC trying to figure out the exact mechanisms that allow humanity to shape the Suprrnal. You have another set of Mysteries with the FC trying to figure out what's been changed already, or reacting to changes that they discover have been made. Finally, you have another set of Mysteries in attempting to discover what the heck humanity is going to do to the Supernal next, and can they shape it into something useful? You need to stop looking at just Techne's utilitarian ends.<br /> <br /> The 6th Watchtower is the Tremere one, the Tower of the Soul. The FC used to be a lot of very young Nameless Orders. The Tremere used to be part of the Diamond and know all the terminology and bring a sense of legitimate, long lasting history. So, what if, instead of just the Seers trying to seduce the Nameless the Tremere were as well? They could do it without having to really worry about the Diamond or Seers noticing. If you really twist their ideology in knots they even have a sort of FC view of the Supernal, they believe that slowly &quot;transforming&quot; the souls of humanity by creating a &quot;connection&quot; between those souls and the 6th Tower will eventually bring about a major change to the Supernal capable of doing things like merging all of the Subtle Arcana together into one super Arcana. Anyway, point is, the Nameless War could have had a lot of Little Refusals to various corrupting influences before getting up to the Great Refusal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, all of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:27:33-08:00","id":1036119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035998-mystery-in-nameless-war?p=1036104#post1036104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'll just repeat myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are repeating yourself because you did not answered my question. I understand that FC, in the end, <i>need</i> to see that Supernal is changing with humanity. I really get this is end result. The problem is HOW to start this question in the first place - <b>HOW one or two Nameless can say 'Well, we can check if magic is really evolving across millenia, maybe our magic can change to?'</b> -<i> Especially</i>, since they are, you know, Nameless, i.e. without formal Orders trening. I could see two Mystygougs analyzing their Athenea milenium old Grimoires and books about how <i>Magic is Alive</i> and seeing pattern with rise of Humanity ( Basically, analyzing proposed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-%E2%80%98growing%E2%80%99-with-humanity\">topic of mine from couple of months</a> ). But I <i>really</i> have a hard time to see the hook on three, four Nameless just saying 'Well, we can study as our magical traditions are better conduits for magic and how this change with Sleepers culture'. I could even see this theory coming from once established semi-official FC groups few years before Great Refusal, when there is enough Nameless in those groups to make connections, seeing past all those crazy inventors, shamans and other left around groups.<br /> <br /> I have just problem with seeing lone PCs at start of the Nameless War to start look in to this phenomena as PC level Mystery and starting the wheel of Techne idea in Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-22-2017, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:45:14-08:00","id":1036128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it's 'Oh, you can use voodoo and psychic projection as your Yantras in magic? That's great!' and Mystery is solved. It does not seem as lasting Mystery too dwell in to, at least for me now. </div> </div> </div>First, I was specifically addressing this, which was your complaint about how Techne doesn't seem mysterious. You didn't state it as a question so I didn't know there was a question to be answered.<br /> <br /> Now that you've actually stated a question, 'how did the development of Techne start to be a thing?' We can start to work on answering that. I think that the most obvious answer is that different Nameless Orders would start to compare notes. Remember they're trying to reject the Diamond and stay at the bleeding edge of magical advancement so they would know that there needs to be a lot of cross-pollinating of ideas. The PCs could be facilitators in this endeavor, being the ones willing to go out and find other Mages that are interacting with radically different, mortal understandings of magic. They have their own system and they can try practicing the new system and then they compare the differences and the similarities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:17:37-08:00","id":1036299,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that in the mundane world an age of discovery is happening, not only scientific but also in regards to ancient and hidden cultures. You don't have to have your Nameless get together and start comparing notes, just have your characters discover the notes left by an ancient culture or those of previously hidden (not global or European) cultures, start to see common patterns and pursue the topic from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T19:42:31-08:00","id":1036407,"title":"","content":"Considering the time fuckery that happens in Mage too, it's entirely possible that some group of Mages happened across a bunch of &quot;ruins&quot; which appear to be from a hyper-advanced civilization the research of which led to the development of Techne.<br /> <br /> In other words, you aren't bound by the limits of reality for explaining something in Mage the way you are in real life, because ultimately, you're playing with a work of fiction. Getting into the weeds can be plenty of fun, but if it hasn't happened &quot;on screen&quot; with your PCs there, then it hasn't happened and can be changed to suit the game and the story in any way you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:49:15-08:00","id":1037239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035998-mystery-in-nameless-war?p=1036119#post1036119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have just problem with seeing lone PCs at start of the Nameless War to start look in to this phenomena as PC level Mystery and starting the wheel of Techne idea in Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, I see Techn\u00e9 as an emergent property of the Order's global ascendancy. There is no single &quot;techn\u00e9&quot; that the FC practices: it's both a philosophy and a general approach to magic and culture, one with many many differences. It's the proverbial elephant and the blind men arguing about it. The answer to this mystery is &quot;Humanity is magical&quot;, but it's not the whole answer, and even to reach there the Nameless columns had to collate and compare many praxes to finally come up with that answer.<br /> <br /> I imagine that there would have existed all sorts of columns, each with its own little nugget of insight. Reaper columns, anarchist columns, scientific-minded columns, masonic lodges, archeomancer columns, &quot;rediscovered&quot; traditionalist cabals, etc. Each and every one of them bring their own obsessions to the nascent Order, but in the end is the political necessity and the historical context that bring the core ethos of the Free Council into being: democracy, revolution and the mystical exaltation of cultural diversity. All other concerns become secondary afterwards, and even violently purged from the Order once the original leadership start consolidating their power.<br /> <br /> My advice is that you should consider the idea that the exploration of techn\u00e9 is really an exploration of magical society, and how mundane society push and pulls against the constraints of accepted magical inquiry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":".  Clarification 01-24-2017, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T14:22:49-08:00","id":1037417,"title":"","content":"To me Techne and 'Humanity is Magical' just seems to be mages recognizing that just as some ancient civilization of wizards once created tools that could serve as supernal symbols, so to do current living cultures. Whatever form it takes be it totem poles or sand paintings, shamans, astrologers and innumerable wise men of different civilizations have tools their own cultures have given supernal meaning. It's a recognition that humanity still has influence over the supernal, or the ability to perceive it in new ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T17:05:32-08:00","id":1038651,"title":"","content":"For me, the big difference between what was thought before Free Council and what is thought after it happened is this:<br /> <br /> Pre-Techne, Mages pretty much assumed that there is unchanging &quot;alphabet&quot; of magical symbols, source and root of all magical expressions. This alphabet is unchanged - it started complete, is complete, and will be complete. All the different ways of doing magic? Nothing new under the Sun. Everything &quot;new&quot; is just a retelling, a new expression of something that was there all along. Only &quot;new&quot; things are things that already existed but wasn't found out yet - or, more probably, it was forgotten and rediscovered. <br /> <br /> Free Council claims that this is untrue. The root alphabet wasn't born complete. It was different 1000 years ago and it's different now and will be different tomorrow. And it's easy to change. Humanity can do it. And because this alphabet describes the world, it *is* the world. If you don't like the world, you can literally change it on fundamental level by introducing something new into it, and will remain there, possibly giving you a chance for better, brighter tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:41:25-08:00","id":1038740,"title":"","content":"And that would be the argument between the Diamond and Free Council in a nut shell.<br /> \u200bJust a thought but maybe for your Chronicle instead of focusing the story around the mystery of the Nameless you could instead focus on the Great Refusal. The book tells us that the Seers saw a way to finally and ultimately defeat the Diamond with the help of the Nameless Orders, perhaps that method and plan could be your mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}